          <p>
            The last row is the one that saves surfaces. When you do not know how something will respond, the answer is always the widest tip from the greatest distance, on a patch that does not show, before you touch anything visible. Thirty seconds there tells you more than any chart can about that material in its current condition.
          </p>

          <p>
            Full pressure guidance by surface, including where the numbers come from and what excess pressure actually does to each material, is in our guide to <a href="/what-psi-pressure-washer-do-i-need/">what PSI you need</a>. For the surfaces where no nozzle is the right answer, see <a href="/what-not-to-pressure-wash/">what not to pressure wash</a>.
